From: Banana <banana@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: q6apm: report the graph close, and how long it took

The graph behind a frontend is torn down by the ADSP, not by the CPU:
audioreach_graph_mgmt_cmd(APM_CMD_GRAPH_CLOSE) goes through
audioreach_send_cmd_sync(), which waits up to 5 s for the DSP's
GPR_BASIC_RSP_RESULT. q6apm_put_audioreach_graph() threw that result away,
so a close the DSP never acknowledged -- the state a frontend opened right
afterwards sees as a half-built graph, and the AW88166 amps then fail to
start ("start failure") -- was completely silent in dmesg. The handover
between the menu and a game (MultiMedia1 released, a game opened into the
same graph id) is exactly where that costs sound.

Log the failure, and the close round-trip when it is slow (>= 50 ms) so the
window is measurable on the unit without CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG (which Banana
does not set). Ordinary closes stay at dev_dbg: the menu reopens its frontend
on every cue, so anything louder would be spam.

This changes no behaviour -- it only makes the one quiet failure visible,
which is what decides whether the userspace "wait one beat" handover still
earns its keep or can come out.

Signed-off-by: Banana <banana@localhost>
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -124,14 +124,31 @@ static void q6apm_put_audioreach_graph(struct kref *ref)
 {
 	struct audioreach_graph *graph;
 	struct q6apm *apm;
+	unsigned long t0;
+	unsigned int ms;
+	int ret;
 
 	graph = container_of(ref, struct audioreach_graph, refcount);
 	apm = graph->apm;
 
-	audioreach_graph_mgmt_cmd(graph, APM_CMD_GRAPH_CLOSE);
+	/*
+	 * The graph is torn down by the ADSP: audioreach_graph_mgmt_cmd() waits for the DSP's
+	 * APM_CMD_GRAPH_CLOSE response (audioreach_send_cmd_sync(), 5 s). That result was thrown
+	 * away, so a close the DSP never acknowledged -- the very state a frontend opened right
+	 * afterwards sees as a half-built graph (the amps then fail to start) -- was silent.
+	 */
+	t0 = jiffies;
+	ret = audioreach_graph_mgmt_cmd(graph, APM_CMD_GRAPH_CLOSE);
+	ms = jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - t0);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(apm->dev, "graph %d: close failed (%d) after %u ms\n", graph->id, ret, ms);
+	else if (ms >= 50)
+		dev_info(apm->dev, "graph %d: close took %u ms\n", graph->id, ms);
+	else
+		dev_dbg(apm->dev, "graph %d: closed after %u ms\n", graph->id, ms);
 
 	mutex_lock(&apm->lock);
 	graph = idr_remove(&apm->graph_idr, graph->id);
 	mutex_unlock(&apm->lock);
 
 	kfree(graph->graph);
 	kfree(graph);
 }
